1208:   fontFamily: "JetBrainsMono",
1209:   fontSize: 11,
1210:   fontWeight: "700",
1211:   textTransform: "uppercase",
1212:   letterSpacing: 0.5,
1213:   color: colors.onSurfaceVariant,
1214:   }}>
```

There is no null guard on `webViewRef.current` beyond the `if` at line 517 (which is fine), and no throttling/dedup beyond `msg.wordWrap !== WORD_WRAP` on the WebView side. When `wordWrap` flips to `true`, a `setWordWrap` postMessage is sent while the existing editor is already alive (so `view && msg.wordWrap !== WORD_WRAP` is true) → enters the destroy+recreate branch → triggers the crash described in §3/§4.

## 3) The `EditorView.lineWrapping` reference + crash path analysis

**File:** `/workspaces/learn-p5/src/utils/editor/exerciseHtml.ts:485`

```
485: var lineWrapping = _CM.EditorView.lineWrapping;
```

This thread's "previous fix" is intact: the bundle defines the static `R.lineWrapping=R.contentAttributes.of({class:"cm-lineWrapping"});` (where `R` is the post-minify name for `EditorView`), AND `EditorView:()=>R` is in the bundle's named-export map (see §4 grep output). So `_CM.EditorView.lineWrapping` correctly resolves to the lineWrapping Extension. The `lineWrapping` local is **not** undefined. Line 624 guards with truthiness (`WORD_WRAP && lineWrapping`), so passing a defined Extension is fine. This is **not** the crash source.

The actual failure is in `computeP5Decos`, which uses the other alias `DecorationSet` (line 482) that IS undefined:

```
528: const p5FnMark = Decoration.mark({ class: 'cm-p5-fn' });
529:
530: function computeP5Decos(v) {
531:   var decos = [];
532:   syntaxTree(v.state).iterate({
533:     enter: function(n) {
534:       if (n.name === 'CallExpression' || n.name === 'NewExpression') {
535:         var callee = n.node.firstChild;
536:         if (callee && callee.name === 'Identifier') {
537:           var name = v.state.sliceDoc(callee.from, callee.to);
538:           if (${JSON.stringify(P5_FUNCTION_NAMES)}.indexOf(name) >= 0) {
539:             decos.push(p5FnMark.range(callee.from, callee.to));
540:           }
541:         }
542:       }
543:     }
544:   });
545:   return DecorationSet.create(v.state, decos);   // <-- TypeError: undefined.create
546: }
```

`computeP5Decos` is invoked from the `ViewPlugin` class constructor:

```
548: function P5FnPlugin(view) { this.decorations = computeP5Decos(view); }
549: P5FnPlugin.prototype.update = function(update) {
550:   if (update.docChanged || update.viewportChanged) {
551:     this.decorations = computeP5Decos(update.view);
552:   }
553: };
554: var p5FnPlugin = ViewPlugin.fromClass(P5FnPlugin, {
555:   decorations: function(v) { return v.decorations; }
556: });
```

`p5FnPlugin` is part of `getExtensions()` (line 614). On the toggle-ON path the handler at line 881 calls `new EditorView({ state: EditorState.create({ doc: savedDoc, extensions: getExtensions() }), ... })`. Inside `new EditorView(...)`, CodeMirror instantiates each `ViewPlugin`'s class with the view — i.e., `new P5FnPlugin(view)` → `computeP5Decos(view)` → `DecorationSet.create(...)` with `DecorationSet === undefined`, throwing `TypeError: Cannot read properties of undefined (reading 'create')`. The uncaught exception bubbles out of `new EditorView` and crashes the WebView's React-Native WebView/render loop. The `lineWrapping` extension itself is never at fault here — the same crash would occur if you flipped word-wrap OFF→ON or ON→OFF; any path that recreates the `EditorView` (or any initial construction that eagerly runs the plugin) hits it.

(Aside: there is no `.catch`, no `try/catch` around `new EditorView` in the handler, so the exception is fatal for the WebView instance.)

## 4) The generated CodeMirror bundle export check

**File:** `/workspaces/learn-p5/src/utils/editor/codemirror-bundle.generated.ts` (2 lines, minified single-line IIFE).

`EditorView` IS exported (good — that's why `_CM.EditorView.lineWrapping` works now), but `DecorationSet` is NOT exported anywhere:

- The bundle's named-export map (the `Xa(t_,{...})` expression near the start) lists:
  `CompletionContext, Decoration, EditorState, EditorView, HighlightStyle, ViewPlugin, autocompletion, basicSetup, indentSelection, javascript, keymap, prettier, prettierPluginAcorn, prettierPluginEstree, syntaxHighlighting, syntaxTree, tags` — `DecorationSet` is absent.
- `grep -c "DecorationSet"` in the generated file → `0`. The string doesn't appear anywhere (it's a TypeScript-only export from `@codemirror/view`, a type with no runtime value).

The bundle's entry source actually does request a re-export:

**File:** `/workspaces/learn-p5/src/utils/editor/bundleEntry.ts`

```
1: import { basicSetup, EditorView } from "codemirror";
2: import { EditorState } from "@codemirror/state";
3: import { keymap, ViewPlugin, Decoration, DecorationSet } from "@codemirror/view";
...
13: export {
14:   basicSetup,
15:   EditorView,
16:   EditorState,
17:   keymap,
18:   syntaxHighlighting,
19:   HighlightStyle,
20:   syntaxTree,
21:   ViewPlugin,
22:   Decoration,
23:   DecorationSet,
24:   indentSelection,
25:   javascript,
26:   tags,
27:   autocompletion,
28:   CompletionContext,
29:   prettier,
30:   prettierPluginEstree,
31:   prettierPluginAcorn,
32: };
```

The entry re-exports `DecorationSet` (line 23), but because `DecorationSet` from `@codemirror/view` is a TypeScript type (no runtime binding), esbuild correctly emits nothing for it when bundling with `--bundle --format=iife` (see `/workspaces/learn-p5/scripts/bundle-editor.mjs:19-22`). So the locally-generated bundle simply can't surface `_CM.DecorationSet`. The current generated bundle predates (or simply excludes) this concern — even though `bundleEntry.ts` lists it, no code actually uses it from the entry, so esbuild tree-shook/had no runtime artifact for it.

So the symptom cascade is:
1. Toggling Word Wrap "On" in `[id].tsx` → posts `{ type:"setWordWrap", wordWrap:true }`.
2. WebView handler (exerciseHtml.ts:875) → `view.destroy()` then `new EditorView({ extensions: getExtensions() })`.
3. `getExtensions()` includes `p5FnPlugin` (exerciseHtml.ts:614).
4. `new EditorView` instantiates `P5FnPlugin(view)` → `computeP5Decos(view)` → `DecorationSet.create(v.state, decos)` (line 545).
5. `DecorationSet` is `undefined` (because `_CM.DecorationSet` is undefined in the bundle) → `TypeError: Cannot read properties of undefined (reading 'create')` thrown synchronously inside `new EditorView`.
6. The crash is unhandled in the WebView → the editor (and likely the whole CodeMirror WebView) seizes up. No fallback recreation or try/catch exists.

## 5) Other `@codemirror/view` Compartment/reconfigure paths

Searched both `src/utils/editor/` and `src/app/learn/` for `wrapCompartment`, `Compartment`, `reconfigure` — **no matches**. The word-wrap feature is the only consumer of `lineWrapping`, and it deliberately uses destroy+recreate rather than `Compartment.reconfigure(...)`. So no `reconfigure(undefined)` crash path exists; the only undefined-extension-related crash is the `DecorationSet.create` one in §3/§4. Other potential consumer: none. The toggle path is the only reconstruction trigger wired up today.

---

## Relevant files (absolute paths)

- `/workspaces/learn-p5/src/utils/editor/exerciseHtml.ts` — handler at L875-895, `lineWrapping`/`DecorationSet` aliases at L482/L485, `computeP5Decos` crash site at L530-546, `getExtensions` at L608-626, `p5FnPlugin` at L548-556.
- `/workspaces/learn-p5/src/app/learn/[course]/[id].tsx` — toggle state L139, postMessage L516-520, persistence L640-641/L673-676, modal UI L1186-1214.
- `/workspaces/learn-p5/src/utils/editor/codemirror-bundle.generated.ts` — `EditorView` exported, `DecorationSet` NOT present (zero occurrences).
- `/workspaces/learn-p5/src/utils/editor/bundleEntry.ts` — re-exports `DecorationSet` (L3, L23) but esbuild strips the type-only import; runtime export absent.
- `/workspaces/learn-p5/scripts/bundle-editor.mjs` — bundling config (`--bundle --format=iife --global-name=CM --minify`), L19-22.

## Recommendation (for the fix, not applied here)

The runtime call `DecorationSet.create(v.state, decos)` at `exerciseHtml.ts:545` should use `Decoration.set(decos)` from the already-working `_CM.Decoration` export (everything else in this codebase already uses `Decoration.mark`/`Decoration.set` from `@codemirror/view`). Concretely, change line 545 to `return Decoration.set(decos);` (the true runtime API), since `DecorationSet` does not exist as a runtime value in `@codemirror/view`. Independent of that, the `setWordWrap` destroy+recreate path (lines 880-888) should additionally be wrapped in a `try/catch` so a plugin failure doesn't permanently wedged the WebView, and `ViewPlugin.define`/`fromClass` decorations returning `Decoration.set([])` for an empty array is fine. No `@codemirror/view` named-export `DecorationSet` will ever be non-undefined at runtime, so regenerating the bundle would not change this symptom.
